{title: The God of Abraham Praise}
{artist: Thomas Olivers (after the Yigdal) / Leoni (Hebrew melody)}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: Em}
{key_original: Fm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: the-god-of-abraham-praise.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (The_God_Of_Abraham_Praise-Yigdal-Leoni)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[B]The [E]God [B]of [Em]Abraham [B]praise,
[Em]Who [Am]reigns enthroned [D]a[G]bove;
[D]An[G]cient of e[C]ver[G]last[D7]ing [Em]days,
[Am]And [G]God__[D7]__ of [G]Love;
[G]Jehovah, great I [D]AM!
[D]By [C]earth and [G]Heav’n [Am]con[B]fessèd;
[B]I [Em]bow [B]and [Em]bless [D]the [G]sa[C]cred [Am]name
[Am]For[Em]ev__[B7]__er [Em]blessed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[B]The [E]God [B]of [Em]Abr'ham [B]praise,
[Em]At [Am]Whose supreme [D]com[G]mand
[D]From [G]earth I rise [C]and [G]seek [D7]the [Em]joys
[Am]At [G]His__[D7]__ right [G]hand;
[G]I all on earth for[D]sake,
[D]Its [C]wisdom, [G]fame, [Am]and [B]pow'r;
[B]And [Em]Him [B]my [Em]on[D]ly [G]Por[C]tion [Am]make,
[Am]My [Em]Shield__[B7]__ and [Em]Tow'r.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[B]The [E]God [B]of [Em]Abraham [B]praise,
[Em]Whose [Am]all suffic[D]ient [G]grace
[D]Shall [G]guide me all [C]my [G]hap[D7]py [Em]days,
[Am]In [G]all__[D7]__ my [G]ways.
[G]He calls a worm His [D]friend,
[D]He [C]calls Him[G]self [Am]my [B]God!
[B]And [Em]He [B]shall [Em]save [D]me [G]to [C]the [Am]end,
[Am]Thro’ [Em]Je__[B7]__sus’ [Em]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[B]He [E]by [B]Him[Em]self has [B]sworn;
[Em]I [Am]on His oath [D]de[G]pend,
[D]I [G]shall, on ea[C]gle [G]wings [D7]up[Em]borne,
[Am]To [G]Heav’n__[D7]__ a[G]scend.
[G]I shall behold His [D]face;
[D]I [C]shall His [G]power [Am]a[B]dore,
[B]And [Em]sing [B]the [Em]won[D]ders [G]of [C]His [Am]grace
[Am]For[Em]ev__[B7]__er[Em]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[B]Tho’ [E]na[B]ture’s [Em]strength de[B]cay,
[Em]And [Am]earth and hell [D]with[G]stand,
[D]To [G]Canaan’s bounds [C]I [G]urge [D7]my [Em]way,
[Am]At [G]His__[D7]__ com[G]mand.
[G]The watery deep I [D]pass,
[D]With [C]Jesus [G]in [Am]my [B]view;
[B]And [Em]thro’ [B]the [Em]how[D]ling [G]wil[C]der[Am]ness
[Am]My [Em]way__[B7]__ pur[Em]sue.
{end_of_verse}
